A||||3||penetrator||E-Brake light||||1||
Z||000000||penetrator||05-14-2001||11:55 AM||||My e brake light dosent lit up anymore when i engage the handle, and when the light aint on i cant open my motorhood without turning the engine off. Probably not a mayor problem, but it is irritating. <BR>Any ideas where to search to fix it?<P>Cheers<BR> <A HREF="http://www.hyperwerks.se/fiero" TARGET=_blank>www.hyperwerks.se/fiero</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Carrolles||05-14-2001||12:37 PM||||I take it that you have a manual transmission?  The electric trunk is not supposed to operate with the engine running in Manual trans cars unless the e-brake is on.<P>It sounds like the E-brake light switch is out of adjustment.  It is located at the base of the E-brake lever underneath the trim that covers the door sill.<P>Try wiggling the e-brake lever to see if it will set the light and enable the switch.||||reg||1
Z||000002||penetrator||05-14-2001||12:39 PM||||Yes, it is a manual.<P>And thanks alot<P>Magnus||||reg||1
Z||000003||mbramble||05-14-2001||12:50 PM||||Yea I ran into a bit of a problem with the e-brake switch on my project car.  I had just put the dash, instrument panel, new headliner, and the over headconsole back in on Sat morning.  Was making sure that all the lights, guages, etc. Worked.  All was well except for 1. my tach -- it swings over to the right side and then kind of falls to the bottom and bangs in to the oil pressure guage!! Bought this cluster from a junkyard for $5.  May have to find a new one. 2. My remote deck lid switch wouldn't work.  Made sure the e-brake was on but still no workee.  I then remembered that I have the harness for the driver's side (e-brake, door ajar) unplugged so I don't have to listen to the blue-thingy when I start the engine (since I have no doors!!).  Plugged it back in and the remote release worked fine. <p>[This message has been edited by mbramble (edited 05-14-2001).]||||reg||1
